 # Project agent instructions
 
+## Friend-published track news override (2026-10-16)
+The owner adds friends' new tracks to Garage News. Show NEW CIRCUIT articles with the publisher, track name and real outline. Capture one shared first-publication fact atomically with verified/legacy publication using one conditional insert; no friend fan-out, backfill or revision spam. Migration0039 follows0038. Explicit cached feed reads merge current friends' recent facts with the existing keyset inbox: bounded100-friend roster, one batched indexed publication read, at most31 eligible candidates/author and31 publication records before outlines. Pending/old/removed/blocked/restricted/hidden tracks are excluded; unfriend clears cached publication stories immediately. Daily comparisons and inactive-account behavior remain, with the existing shared100-row/minute expiry budget. Backend78 domain+2 HTTP pass with4 SQLite concurrency skips, final single-statement publication37/2skip, client23/HTTP11+14/native79+79/parser820/Ruff pass; initial fixture failures are retained. See `docs/GARAGE_FRIEND_PUBLICATIONS_2026_10_16.md` for actual checks, previews, source hashes and task-only patch. Owner/phone acceptance and matching API/worker/client/migration rollout remain; no phone/APK/deployment.
+
 ## Backend product analysis and monitoring review (2026-10-16)
 The owner requests a review and steps for top-tier player behaviour, game quality, production monitoring and monetisation analysis. Deployed revision59/schema36 has useful bounded inspectors, but needs shared metric/coverage definitions, independent continuous alarms/incidents, segmentable cohorts, release comparisons, real financial/economy sources and safe experiments. Existing all-player Studio totals remain required; separately labelled business populations need an explicit policy decision. Read-only90 browser+8 inspector observations, four isolated correctness reproductions and owned PostgreSQL10k/50k profiles are recorded with per-view dispositions and gated backlog in `docs/BACKEND_PRODUCT_REVIEW_2026_10_16.md`. This is analysis only, not authorisation to implement/deploy the roadmap. No runtime source edits, live data mutations, phone check/test or APK action.
 
